    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d145">

                <pb facs="0309" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v04/pg283"/>

                <head>145. Memorandum of Telephone Conversation Between the Under Secretary of State
                    for Political Affairs (Harriman) and Michael V. Forrestal of the National
                    Security Council Staff<anchor n="1" xml:id="d145-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            type="conversation-or-meeting-date" when="1963-09-23"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">September 23,
                    1963</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Forrestal asked if there were any last minute instructions. Harriman said to
                    reserve State’s position. Say they can’t speak for State.</p>
                <p>Harriman mentioned that he listened to CBS this morning and got the flavor of the
                    lady who is coming here.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d145-f2"/> He said he was worried.
                    He said she said she was a true friend because she was telling us where we made
                    our mistakes.</p>
                <p>Harriman said it was important that no one official see her.</p>
                <p>Harriman said he thought he would talk to one or two people about this. He said
                    he would talk to Al Friendly.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d145-f3"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d145-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d145-f1-content">
